 "notes": {
  "https://www.aft.org/ae/fall2013/dunlosky": "Effects in classrooms are usually smaller than in the laboratory. Research Bite #84 beside it shows by how much.",
  "https://www.cis.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/AP55-update.pdf": "A think-tank paper, not peer reviewed. Read it with the NSW literature review beside it.",
  "https://features.apmreports.org/sold-a-story/": "A journalism series from the United States, in several episodes. It is not research.",
  "https://www.ollielovell.com/judithhochman/": "The Writing Revolution is widely used but has had little formal evaluation. Karen Harris's SRSD, in the full list, has stronger trial evidence.",
  "https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/ED500486.pdf": "Long, and from 2008. Its strongest findings on explicit teaching are for students who struggle.",
